# {{ project-name }}

> A {{ unit_kind }} unit operation for the [tpt-process](https://github.com/tpt-solutions/tpt-process) suite.

Scaffolded with `cargo generate --path templates/unit-op-crate` from the
`tpt-process` repository. It implements [`UnitBehavior`] — the contract the
flowsheet solver executes — so the unit registers into a `UnitRegistry` and
runs inside any `tpt-process` flowsheet.

## Fill in your physics

Everything lives in `src/lib.rs` between the `BEGIN PHYSICS` / `END PHYSICS`
markers. House rules (see CONTRIBUTING.md in tpt-process):

- SI units everywhere; state that anything else in the docs.
- No panics in library code: return `UnitError` (typed) instead.
- Deterministic: same inputs, same outputs.
- Keep the `ports_match_trait_contract`, `solve_returns_the_right_outlet_count`,
  and `wrong_inlet_count_is_an_error_not_a_panic` tests passing.

